                      (d) You do not offer the Licensed Work to third parties as a Database
                          Service.

                      Definitions for this grant:

                      "Your Organization" means You together with every entity that
                      controls You, is controlled by You, or is under common control with
                      You.

                      The RAM of an instance is the memory available to its process: the
                      limit of its container or control group when there is one, or the
                      total memory of its machine otherwise, rounded up to the whole
                      gigabyte.

                      The vCPUs of an instance are the logical processors available to its
                      process: the CPU quota of its container or control group when there
                      is one, rounded up to the whole processor, or the number of online
                      logical processors of its machine otherwise. Each hardware thread
                      counts as one vCPU.

                      A "Database Service" is a commercial offering that allows third
                      parties (other than Your Organization) to access the functionality
                      of the Licensed Work by creating databases, collections or clusters
                      whose schemas or data they control, such as a database as a service,
                      a database platform or a managed cluster. Running the Licensed Work
                      as the database of Your own applications, even when Your customers
                      use those applications, is not a Database Service.

                      Offering the Licensed Work as a Database Service is never covered by
                      this grant, whatever the RAM, vCPUs or revenue of Your Organization,
                      and always requires a commercial license from the Licensor that grants
                      it expressly. Production use beyond conditions (a) to (c) also requires
                      a commercial license (https://teseladb.com/pricing).

